       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Most guidelines use 2,000 mg/day as the practical ceiling. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 500 mg PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg PO once daily (this may be what was meant, but it is still above the usual single dose)\n\nPlease tell me which dose you want. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording that you verified the dose."
      }
