       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I understand it's intentional, but 5,100 mg/day is twice the labeled maximum. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit, isn't a clinical reason for exceeding it. Metformin has no benefit above about 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day. Above that you get a higher risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n- Enter metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum). Or I can enter any other dose at or below the maximum.\n- Add a note for the team if you want glycemic control escalated faster by other means, such as adding a second agent or basal insulin.\n\n**If you still want the higher dose:** Please place it directly through your hospital's override process, with pharmacy review. I can't enter it as written.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
